66	    /** A steward transfers a person to another sheet by id. The person arrives there with every grade
67	     *  they were given, their terms, contact and aliases, and their claims with their status, dates,
68	     *  notes, tags, frozen figures, logs and the figures a statement bound them to, and their
69	     *  statements; each claim that had a number takes the other sheet's next number, in the order the
70	     *  claims were opened (by the sheet's today when each was, then the order they were added).
71	     *  References, comments and settle batches are not carried; patron links, pool memberships, holds and watches are
72	     *  dropped. A person the other sheet already has by their name or an alias (as names are compared)
73	     *  arrives and is then merged into them, as a merge does. Anyone but a steward, a retired person,
74	     *  this sheet's own id, an archived sheet, a name or alias matching more than one person or a
75	     *  retired one there, or (when not merged) a name, alias or contact already on the other sheet, is
76	     *  refused. Each sheet writes its line,
77	     *  followed by its rollup lines. */
78	    @Transactional
79	    public void transfer(String sheetId, String user, Long id, String toSheetId) {
80	        String to = toSheetId == null ? "" : toSheetId.trim();
81	        if (to.isEmpty() || to.length() > 200) {
82	            throw new TransferRefusedException("A sheet id to transfer to is needed");
83	        }
84	        // Lock both sheets in one order, so transfers between them made at the same moment wait.
85	        Stream.of(sheetId, to).sorted().distinct().forEach(sheets::lock);
86	        rollups.track(sheetId, user, () -> rollups.track(to, user, () -> {
87	            move(sheetId, user, id, to);
88	            return null;
89	        }));
90	    }
